    wp_register_script(
        'my-block-script',
        get_template_directory_uri() . '/js/my-block.js',
        array( 'wp-blocks', 'wp-element', 'wp-editor' )
    );

    wp_register_style(
        'my-block-styles',
        get_template_directory_uri() . '/css/my-block.css'
    );

    register_block_type( 'my-block' );
}
add_action( 'init', 'register_my_block' );
```

### Step 2: Define the Block Attributes

In the JavaScript file associated with your block, you'll define the block's attributes. This includes the heading, paragraph, and image. You'll use the `registerBlockType` function from the `wp.blocks` namespace to define the block.

```javascript
